{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "two-axis reflection-symmetric color pattern with green placeholder pixels",
  "transform": "replace each green pixel with the unique non-green color in its horizontal/vertical reflection orbit; keep all other pixels unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16x16 (fixed)
  output_pattern:
    symmetry: full D4 (LR + UD + both diagonals + 90/180/270 rotations)
    colors: 5-8 non-black non-green colors; no black or green in output
    structure: 36 D4 orbits (8 of size 4, 28 of size 8), each uniform color
    complexity: avg 8-11 color transitions per row [observed]
  green_damage:
    count: 2 rectangular blobs totaling 10-20 green cells
    blob_dims: each blob is 2-4 rows x 2-4 cols (perfect rectangle, fill_ratio=1.0)
    blob_area: 4-12 cells per blob
    placement: blobs may span quadrant boundaries; scattered across grid
    orbit_constraint: at most 2 green cells per LR+UD reflection orbit (size-4 orbit)
    solver_recovery: each LR+UD orbit with green retains >=2 non-green cells of identical color

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first then damage
  steps:
    1. Generate the D4-symmetric 16x16 output by filling the 36-cell fundamental domain (upper-left triangle of TL quadrant) with 5-8 random non-black non-green colors, then reflecting to full grid.
    2. Place 2 rectangular green blobs (each 2-4 x 2-4) at random positions. Verify that no LR+UD orbit (4-cell group) has more than 2 cells covered by green across both blobs combined. Retry placement if violated.
    3. Replace blob cells with GREEN to produce the input.
```
</generation_spec>
