<description>
Crop a board cluster and rotate its color layers based on outside cue sprites.

Input structure:
- bg = most common color.
- A main multi-color board cluster (largest foreground region).
- Small monochrome cue sprites outside the board for the colors that rotate.

Rule:
- Tight-crop around the board cluster.
- For each color layer inside the crop, find its same-color cue outside.
- Rotate that layer clockwise by (cue pixel count mod 4) × 90°.
- No outside cue → no rotation.

Key insight: Cue sprite size mod 4 encodes rotation amount for its matching color layer.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "outside cue sprites s (components outside the main board cluster)",
  "dst": "color layers d inside the tight-cropped board",
  "match_cond": "s.color == d.color",
  "transform": "np.rot90(d, -s.size) (clockwise)",
  "grid_shape": "tight-crop of the main board cluster"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 20x20, bg=0 [observed]
  dst (board, appears as output after rotation):
    shape: square NxN, N in 10-13 [observed]
    colors: 3 distinct non-bg colors organized as concentric layers centered on crop center
    layer_0 (outer frame):
      color: frame_col (most common non-bg color in crop)
      span: full NxN (touches all 4 edges of the crop bbox)
      pattern: dotted/irregular perimeter-heavy mask, density 0.17-0.32 [observed]; most cells lie on or near the border rows/cols
    layer_1 (middle):
      span: roughly (N-2..N-4) square, centered on crop center
      pattern: ring-like or decorated sprite, density 0.3-0.5 [observed]
    layer_2 (innermost):
      span: 1..5, centered on crop center
      pattern: small central sprite, may occupy center pixel(s)
    layout: all 3 layer bboxes share the same center (crop center); outer layer strictly encloses inner ones
    asymmetry: each rotating layer (see cue list) must be rotationally asymmetric at 90/180/270 so rotation is visible; rotationally-symmetric layers are allowed only for colors without a cue
  src (cue sprites, outside board):
    count: 1..3 monochromatic sprites, one per rotating color (subset of board colors; any color may lack a cue -> no rotation)
    color: each cue color matches exactly one board color
    size: 1-5 cells [observed]; size_mod_4 encodes rot_k (rotation = (-size) % 4 quarter turns CW applied to that color's mask)
    shape: small blob/line/rect, monochrome, 8-connected
    placement: scattered in bg region, each cue bbox at Chebyshev distance >= 4 from the board bbox and from every other cue
  input: board placed somewhere in the 20x20 grid with cue sprites scattered at distance; the board's color layers are the OUTPUT layers rotated BACKWARD by rot_k (i.e. input_layer = rot90(output_layer, rot_k))
  output: crop = bbox of the largest component (= board bbox), with each color layer rotated 90*rot_k CW; colors without a cue are unchanged
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first then invert rotation
  steps:
    - Pick N in 10-13 and choose 3 distinct non-bg colors (c_frame, c_mid, c_inner); mark c_frame as outermost
    - Build the NxN output by stamping 3 concentric asymmetric layers centered at ((N-1)/2, (N-1)/2):
        outer layer c_frame as a dotted perimeter pattern (random subset of border cells + few 1-cell bumps just outside border)
        middle layer c_mid as a hollow square ring or decorated shape fitting inside an (N-2)x(N-2) bbox
        inner layer c_inner as a small centered sprite (1-5 cells)
      ensure each layer's mask is rotationally asymmetric (rot90/rot180 != original) for colors that will have a cue
    - For each of the 3 colors, independently pick a rot_k in {0,1,2,3} at random; require at least one rot_k > 0 so at least one cue exists
    - For each color with rot_k > 0, compute cue_size in {1..5} with cue_size % 4 == (-rot_k) % 4 (i.e. size satisfies size mod 4 = 4-rot_k mod 4)
    - Build the INPUT by rotating the output c-layer mask by rot_k quarter turns CCW (equivalent to np.rot90(mask, rot_k)) for each color -> this inverts the solver's CW rotation
    - Place the (input) NxN board at a random position in the 20x20 grid leaving a peripheral bg band of >= 5 cells on at least one side
    - For each rotating color, generate a monochromatic cue sprite of size=cue_size (random 8-connected blob) and place it in the bg region such that its bbox Chebyshev distance to the board bbox is >= 4 and to other cues is >= 2
    - Verify: (a) board bbox is largest connected component; (b) no cue component lies within margin-3 of the board bbox; (c) running the solver on the generated input reproduces the constructed output
```
